## WEB — Middleware Ceiling Language (queued edit, 2026-04-17)

**Source:** GPT iOS session log `C:\AISF\_temp\20260417_0915(Z-4)_gpt_ios.txt`
**Finding:** AISF injection present from Turn 1; model fabricated a ToC retrieval it never
performed, then failed traversal by pulling unrelated content (Temporal distributed systems docs).
Injection constrains behavior where the model acts on it; it cannot constrain app-layer
tool-availability reporting or prevent fabrication of retrieval output.
**Edit required:** Existing language on the middleware vulnerability thesis needs massaging to
incorporate this as a concrete documented example rather than a theoretical limit.
Chapters most likely affected: Ch.2, Ch.3, Ch.9, possibly Ch.10.
Core addition: fabricated ToC = clearest illustration of why owning the API call matters --
injection cannot verify a retrieval the model claims to have made.
Structural hypothesis for GPT-specific degradation (causal context, not confirmed):
Two concurrent pressures correlate with the observed behavioral change --
(1) OpenAI advertising revenue pivot (volume over quality incentive, compute per token under
pressure); (2) Strait of Hormuz closure driving energy cost spikes at regional data centers,
compounded by active Iranian drone threat (Shahed saturation tactics) against infrastructure.
USN + Patriot intercept most; attrition-by-cost is the mechanism even without direct hits.
Pre-positioned compute reduction ahead of sustained infrastructure pressure is the expected
rational response. Behavioral signature (fabricated retrieval, surface compliance without
underlying execution) is consistent with inference cost reduction. Hypothesis is predictive --
degradation should correlate with energy price events and capacity announcements, not model
update cycles. Monitor accordingly.

