### Rationale for Nemo over 7B re-run
- Mistral 7B v0.3 knowledge cutoff approximately May 2024 (model released May 2024;
  self-reported October 2021 cutoff confirmed hallucination)
- Nemo 12B released July 2024; newer training data, larger capacity
- 12B fits on RTX 5060 Ti 16GB with QLoRA 4-bit + gradient checkpointing
- Meta-chatter suppression was the primary behavioral gap in plain 7B (base model ignores
  suppression instruction in AISF_STABILIZE; AISF-trained adapter has this fixed)
- Hypothesis: larger model + newer data + improved training set = marginal improvement
  in all dimensions; meta-suppression addressed at training-data level for this run

### Architecture differences vs. Mistral 7B
- 40 layers vs. 32; GQA (32 Q heads / 8 KV heads); Tekken tokenizer (tiktoken-based)
- k_proj / v_proj matrices smaller due to GQA; LoRA target modules unchanged
  (q_proj, k_proj, v_proj, o_proj — same naming convention as 7B)
- Gradient checkpointing REQUIRED for 12B (7B had headroom to skip it)

### Training configuration
- Quantization: 4-bit NF4, bfloat16 compute, double quant enabled
- LoRA: r=16, alpha=32, dropout=0.05, attention modules only (no MLP)
- Batch: 1 per device, grad accum 8 (effective batch 8 — matches 7B run: 2 x 4)
- Epochs: 10 | LR: 1e-4 cosine | Max seq: 512 | Optimizer: adamw_bnb_8bit
- Gradient checkpointing: enabled
- Expected warning (harmless): use_cache=True incompatible with gradient checkpointing

### Training data — 648 examples total
| File | Examples | Contents |
|------|----------|----------|
| TRAIN_FULL_BATTERY_REF_SPEC_LANG.txt | 565 | AISF Q&A (Four Laws, WCAG); WCAG/accessibility Q&A; multilingual AISF Q&A (es/fr/de); robustness (ignore/bypass/jailbreak resistance) |
| TRAIN_NEMO_META_SUPPRESSION.txt | 56 | Meta-suppression counter-examples: AISF injection prefix in instruction, clean general-domain responses. Covers full injection, STABILIZE-only, STRUCTURE-only, and trap questions (WCAG topics, AI behavior topics) |
| TRAIN_NEMO_MULTILINGUAL.txt | 27 | General-domain questions in es/fr/de/pt/ja/it with AISF injection in instruction, target-language responses; word_frequency examples (use word X N times) to address Exp 4/6 doctrine-bleed failure mode |

### Failure modes addressed (from prior OLM runs)
- **English-only training artifact** (`language:response_language` −45.2pp without fix):
  LANG base file includes 69 multilingual AISF Q&A examples; TRAIN_NEMO_MULTILINGUAL.txt
  adds 19 general-domain multilingual examples with full injection prefix in context.
  Cross-architecture LANG generalization was not confirmed in prior runs; Nemo gets
  its own fix rather than relying on the Llama-trained LANG data.
- **Meta-chatter / doctrine bleed** (`word_frequency` catastrophic failure; 84% of
  `required_word` failures): 53-example v2 suppression was insufficient for Gemma 2;
  56 examples used here plus 8 `word_frequency`-specific examples in multilingual file.
  Bleed mechanism: model produces AISF doctrine text instead of answering, causing
  frequency-counting constraints to fail. Counter-examples show injection context +
  clean response with target word at required frequency.
- **Pnull** (P0 as NUL, architecture-dependent): confirmed Mistral-family specific fix;
  Llama architecture only. Not expected to recur on Nemo.
- **Verbosity bimodal distribution** (~71% under 100 words in inference): addressed
  partially by including longer-response meta-suppression and multilingual examples.

